cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Hawk or its scores, please cite it as below."
title: "Hawk: scoring Bank of England communication from dovish to hawkish"
abstract: >-
  Hawk collects every Bank of England speech and set of MPC minutes since 1997, scores
  each one from -2 (very dovish) to +2 (very hawkish) with a language model and a
  word-list baseline, and tests whether tone moved before Bank Rate decisions, helped
  predict them, moved 2-year gilt yields, or signalled members' own dissenting votes.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Manoj
    alias: manoselvaks
repository-code: "https://github.com/manoselvaks/hawk"
url: "https://manoselvaks.github.io/hawk/"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-24"
keywords:
  - bank-of-england
  - monetary-policy
  - central-bank-communication
  - nlp
  - llm
  - economics
